{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqYJnN9Wii2t3bzJxbgm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This sitting approved nothing and re-anchored nothing. Both verdicts are committed in 7a93110c (trailer `WI: WI-846`), but the re-anchoring snapshot was refused and no registry changed.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=7`.** Every amended row in the SR-227 chain changed what it requires. Of the seven, I'd bless three and not the other four:\n\n- **Would bless TC-268, TC-323 and TC-324.** Each adds a closed, observable case that matches SR-227's amended text.\n- **SR-227 (not blessed):** the refusal for an ordinary dedicated home got weaker. It used to refuse before any launch, home creation, lease or record write, and name the setup step. Now it only refuses \"before retained state changes\", and the Requirement just says to \"preserve\" that refusal, which points at text the row no longer contains.\n- **LLR-270 (not blessed):** the reset, drain, clear-point, lineage and keep-warm rules were replaced with \"remain as before\", which will mean nothing once re-anchored. \"Store-lock contention is outside this row\" also leaves the tombstone mechanism with no specification, even though it is still in the code and still tested. WI-858, which decision D-005 hands that work to, has not been filed.\n- **LLR-305 (not blessed):** the exact Codex sign-in probe outputs that count as signed in or not, and the rule that the probe never creates a missing home, were dropped. No row holds them now, yet TC-323 still asserts \"only documented exit-and-output pairs\".\n- **TC-267 (not blessed):** it dropped the assertions about the dedicated Codex home, the tombstone under a held lock, lock exclusion and leftover files. The tests behind them still exist, but no test case claims them.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=1` (TC-330).** Two problems:\n- Its Expected cell claims no saved or displayed artifact contains the token. That is broader than the verbatim-only limit, and decision D-002 deliberately leaves the CLI's own transcript out.\n- Its Method says \"run the retained-credential tests\" without naming them, and asserts nothing about argv or commits.\n\nIts status stays `Drafted`.\n\n**Follow-ups:** three drafts are in a new `## Dispositions` section of the WI-846 spec, and intake mints them at this lane's merge. They were drafted there rather than in the verdict file because intake reads them from the spec. They are:\n1. Re-close SR-227's ordinary-home refusal.\n2. Restore LLR-270, LLR-305 and TC-267 to fully stated rules, and give store-lock contention a real home.\n3. Bound TC-330's Expected claim and name its tests and assertions.\n\n**Snapshot refused:** `intake.py snapshot --reattests TC-268,TC-323,TC-324` failed because TC-267's Method has drifted in the same registry, and I judged TC-267 not blessable. I did not add it to `--reattests`. TC-268, TC-323 and TC-324 stay un-anchored until TC-267 is corrected and judged; schedule them in the same sitting. Nothing was written and there is no approval commit.\n\nI left the coordinator's untracked `001-ADJUDICATE-6553682.md.requested` file alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":109699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f747aa98-db01-4369-8ef7-8f3200823751","uuid":"288837c3-32e7-4b68-9432-1ebd143b7e60","timestamp":"2026-10-08T22:14:39.518Z","request_id":"req_011CfqYJn6HBsq5yH1GfmMyz"}
